SIGHT TUTOR — RECREATION SPECIFICATION
======================================

A standalone Python 3 sight-reading trainer. One file (sightread.py), no tkinter,
no ABC. Recreate behavior from this spec; do not invent extra features unless
needed to make the listed ones work.


1. PURPOSE
----------
Teach piano sight-reading on a grand staff. The user plays pitches with QWERTY
(site.key), mouse on an on-screen 88-key piano, or USB MIDI. Notes scroll left
across three bars. A quiz scores hits if the correct pitch is played before the
note leaves the middle "hit zone." Songs load/save as Standard MIDI. An
in-process additive synthesizer produces all audio.


2. RUNTIME AND DEPENDENCIES
---------------------------
- Python 3.9+
- pygame (display, events, mixer, optional pygame.midi)
- numpy (synthesis)
- Standard library only otherwise: json, os, random, struct, dataclasses

No tkinter. File dialogs are drawn in pygame. Create songs/ at startup if missing.


3. CONSTANTS
------------
Default window:     1480 x 920, resizable, minimum 1100 x 700
FPS:                60
Visible bars:       3
Beats per bar:      4
Default BPM:        40 (clamp 20-240)
Sample rate:        44100, stereo, 16-bit
Mixer channels:     32
Piano range:        MIDI 21-108 (A0-C8)
Quiz default pool:  MIDI 36-84
Middle C:           60
PPQ (MIDI write):   480
HUD height:         118 px
Quiz length:        1-500, default 100, stepper uses step 5
Simultaneous voices: 1-8

Colors: dark HUD; cream staff paper; black ink; green hit notes; red misses;
blue ghost notes; orange current playback note.


4. PERSISTENCE FILES (working directory)
----------------------------------------

settings.json
{
  "bpm": 40,
  "simultaneous": 1,
  "instrument": "Piano",
  "limit_to_keymap": false,
  "quiz_length": 100,
  "key": "C",
  "use_song": false,
  "preview": true,
  "quiz_style": "Random",
  "offkey": false,
  "win_w": 1480,
  "win_h": 920,
  "last_dir": "<absolute path to songs/>"
}
If last_dir is missing or not a directory, use songs/ (create it).
Save window size on resize and on quit.

site.key
One mapping per line: <character><midi> with no separator.
Examples: z48    -82
# starts a comment.
Keys are lowercased.
Lookup must happen BEFORE treating "-" as BPM-down.

custom_tones.json
List of Patch dicts. Merge into the instrument combo after built-ins.
A custom patch with the same name replaces the previous custom patch.

songs/
Default load/save folder. MIDI only: .mid and .midi.
Remember last used folder after a successful load/save or after the user
navigates in the file dialog.


5. WINDOW TITLE
---------------
No song:     Sight Tutor
After load/save/record with a title:
             Sight Tutor - <basename without extension>
Abbreviate names longer than about 22 characters with an ellipsis.


6. UI LAYOUT
------------
Top bar (~118 px)

Row 1, left to right:
  Title text
  Buttons: Record, Play, Stop, Load, Save,
           Start N-note quiz (or "Start song quiz" if Use song is on),
           Synthesizer, Help
  Far right: BPM minus button, BPM value, BPM plus button

Row 2:
  Instrument combo
  Key combo (major keys listed below)
  Quiz-style combo: Random, Chords, Progressions, Arpeggios, Mixed
  Voices stepper 1-8
  Quiz/record length stepper
  Checkboxes: site.key, Use song, half-vol, off-key acc.
  Status text

Middle of window:
  Cream grand staff. Treble clef on the upper staff, bass clef on the lower.
  Three equal bars. The MIDDLE bar is the hit zone (light green wash and
  a "hit zone" label).
  Key signature drawn after each clef.
  Notes fly from the right edge of the staff to the left and disappear past
  the left edge.

Bottom third:
  Full 88-key piano, clickable. White keys show C names.
  Held / recently played keys highlight.

Dialogs overlay the window: Synthesizer, Help, File, Quiz results.


7. WIDGETS (custom pygame, no toolkit)
--------------------------------------
Implement: Button, ComboBox (scrollable drop list), Stepper (- value +),
CheckBox, Slider, TextField, modal FileDialog, HelpDialog, SynthDialog.

File dialog rules:
- Modes: load and save.
- List [..] and subfolders as [name], then .mid / .midi files.
- Single-click a file: select it and put the name in the text field.
- Double-click a file: load it (load mode).
- Double-click a folder or [..]: enter that directory.
- songs/ button jumps to the default songs folder.
- Load must refuse paths that are not real files. Never invent a fallback song.
- Save appends .mid if there is no extension. Create parent folders if needed.
- Persist the dialog folder as last_dir.


8. INPUT
--------
1. If event.unicode (lowercased) is in site.key, play that MIDI number.
   Do this BEFORE BPM shortcuts so "-" can be a mapped key.
2. Mouse down on a piano key plays it; mouse up releases the highlight.
3. USB MIDI note-on (status 0x90, velocity > 0) if pygame.midi exists.
   If import fails, print a short message and continue with no MIDI input.
4. Arrow keys change BPM:
     Left / Right  = +/- 1
     Up / Down     = +/- 2
     Shift+Up/Down = +/- 10
   On-screen - / + buttons = +/- 2
5. Esc quits unless a dialog consumes Esc.


9. MUSIC NOTATION
-----------------
Major keys:
  C  G  D  A  E  B  F#  C#  F  Bb  Eb  Ab  Db  Gb  Cb

Sharp order: F C G D A E B
Flat order:  B E A D G C F
Flat keys:   F Bb Eb Ab Db Gb Cb

Draw the correct count of sharps or flats on BOTH staves at conventional
vertical positions (treble and bass placements differ).

Spelling a MIDI pitch in the selected key:
- Use a sharp-spelling table or a flat-spelling table depending on whether
  the key is in the flat-key set.
- Compare the spelled accidental to the key signature for that LETTER.
- If they differ, draw a courtesy accidental ONLY on that notehead:
  sharp, flat, or natural.
- That accidental does NOT persist for the rest of the measure.

Vertical placement:
- MIDI < 60  -> bass staff
- MIDI >= 60 -> treble staff
- Diatonic step = octave * 7 + index of letter in C D E F G A B
- Y = staff_top + 4 * spacing - steps * (spacing / 2)
- Draw ledger lines above and below as needed.

Note duration drawing (FlyingNote.dur in beats):
  dur >= 3.6   whole note:  open head, no stem
  dur >= 1.75  half note:   open head + stem
  dur >  0.6   quarter:     filled head + stem
  dur <= 0.6   eighth:      filled head + stem + flag


10. SCROLLING AND TIMING
------------------------
Staff width maps to 3 bars * 4 beats at the current BPM:

  pixels_per_second = staff_width / (12 * 60 / bpm)

Notes spawn at staff_right - 18 and move left at that speed.

Hit rule:
  correct MIDI number
  AND quiz note not already hit or missed
  AND note.x >= left edge of the middle bar
After that edge, mark the note missed.

Ghost note:
  When the user plays during a quiz, flash a translucent blue note in the
  hit zone for 1 second at the pitch they actually played.

Half-volume preview (checkbox, default ON):
  The first time a quiz note's x crosses into the middle bar, play that
  pitch at channel volume 0.5. This does not count as a hit.


11. SONG MODEL
--------------
SongNote(beat: float, midi: int, dur: float = 1.0)
Song(title, key, bpm, notes[])

Sort notes by (beat, midi).
Group notes whose beats differ by < 1e-4 into simultaneous events.

MIDI write:
  SMF type 0, one track, PPQ 480
  Tempo meta 0xFF 0x51
  Note-on  0x90 velocity 100
  Note-off 0x80
  End of track
  VLQ delta times

MIDI read:
  Accept only files whose bytes start with MThd. Reject anything else.
  Parse ALL tracks.
  Handle running status.
  Note-on with velocity 0 counts as note-off.
  Unpaired note-ons get duration 1.0.
  Read tempo meta for BPM.
  Do NOT support ABC.


12. RECORD / PLAY / STOP
------------------------
Record:
  Clear the in-memory song.
  Capture each user pitch at beat = elapsed_seconds * bpm / 60, duration 1.0.
  Stop when count reaches the quiz-length stepper, or Stop is pressed,
  or Record is pressed again.
  The Record button blinks bright red while recording.
  After a non-empty stop from completing the count, open Save in last_dir
  (or songs/).

Play:
  Copy song.sorted_notes() to a frozen play_list.
  Advance play_beat += dt * bpm / 60.
  When note.beat <= play_beat, play the sound and spawn a flying note
  using that note's duration.
  Highlight the latest spawned note as current.
  Stop when all notes have been spawned AND no non-ghost notes remain
  on the staff.

Stop:
  Ends recording, playback, and quiz.
  If a quiz was running, open the score dialog immediately.


13. QUIZ MODES
--------------
Checkbox "Use song":
  ON + song in memory:
    Quiz events = grouped MIDI events with REAL beats and durations
    (same schedule as Play). Do not force quarter notes.
  ON + empty song:
    Status "No song in memory". Do not start.
  OFF:
    Generate a random quiz of quiz_length notes using style + voices + key.

Random styles (scale = major scale pitch classes of the selected key):

  Random:
    "voices" simultaneous notes, usually in-key, 1 beat each.

  Chords:
    Triad (extra voices stacked in thirds / next octaves) from a random
    scale degree, duration 2 beats.

  Progressions:
    Cycle patterns such as I-V-vi-IV, I-IV-V-I, ii-V-I, I-vi-IV-V.
    Same voicing idea, 2 beats.

  Arpeggios:
    Chord tones one after another, 0.5 beats each, random up or down.

  Mixed:
    Pick one of the above styles per event.

off-key acc. checkbox:
  About 28% chance to shift a generated pitch by +/- 1 semitone
  (or +/- 2 if the first shift is still in key).

site.key only:
  If checked and the map is non-empty, Random style samples from mapped
  MIDI numbers. Other styles still prefer the musical key unless limited.

Scoring:
  +1 per correct pitch before leaving the hit zone.
  Simultaneous chord tones each need their own correct key.
  End when every event is spawned and no pending quiz notes remain,
  or when Stop is pressed.
  Dialog shows: score / total (percent).


14. SYNTHESIZER
---------------
Patch fields:
  name, attack, decay, sustain,
  h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7, h8,
  inharm, noise, vib_rate, vib_depth, fm, detune,
  pair, pair_mix,
  pan_rate, pan_depth, pan_square,
  chorus_rate, chorus_depth, chorus_mix,
  trem_rate, trem_depth, trem_square,
  phaser_rate, phaser_depth,
  delay_time, delay_mix, distortion,
  wah_rate, wah_depth

Built-in instrument names (keep these):
  Piano, Church Organ, Inca Flute, Charango, Banjo, Violin, Sci-Fi Organ,
  Guitar, Human Voice, Sitar, Koto, Harp, Flute, Trumpet, Cello,
  Synth Pad, Space Echo, Leslie, Theremin, Distortion Guitar, Bass Guitar,
  Ukulele, Marimba, Kalimba, Choir Aahs, Saxophone, Clarinet, Handpan,
  FM Bell, Organ Combo

Render about 1.7 seconds mono:
  Sum harmonics i = 1..8 at freq * i * (1 + inharm * (i-1)), optional FM phase.
  Add noise.
  Vibrato amplitude modulation.
  Envelope: min(t/attack, 1) * exp(-decay * max(t-attack, 0)) mixed with sustain.
  Distortion: tanh.
  Tremolo LFO (sine mixed with square).
  Chorus: modulated short delay mix.
  Delay: single echo.
  Stereo: pan LFO left/right; otherwise equal-power mono-to-stereo.
  Optional pair: mix a second named patch at pair_mix.
  Normalize, convert to int16, pygame.sndarray.make_sound.
  Cache sounds by (instrument name, midi).

Synth dialog:
  Sliders for numeric fields, name field, pair combo,
  Save (writes custom_tones.json and adds the name to the instrument combo),
  Preview (MIDI 60), Close.


15. PROGRAM STRUCTURE
---------------------
Suggested types:
  Patch, Song, SongNote, FlyingNote, Piano, Tutor,
  plus widgets and MIDI helpers.

Tutor.run loop:
  handle events
  update(dt)
  draw
On quit: save settings, close MIDI input.

Graceful MIDI absence. Never crash on missing optional files.


16. BEHAVIORAL CHECKLIST
------------------------
[ ] songs/ is created; last folder is remembered; missing last folder -> songs/
[ ] MIDI load/save only; file content must start with MThd
[ ] File list click updates the text box; no phantom default song
[ ] Song quiz uses MIDI beats and durations; Play and song-quiz timing match
[ ] Random quiz styles + 1-8 voices + off-key accidentals
[ ] Accidentals drawn per note vs current key signature only
[ ] Stop ends quiz (score), play, and record; Record blinks while armed
[ ] Half-volume preview when a quiz note enters the middle bar
[ ] Ghost note shows the pitch the user actually played
[ ] Caption is Sight Tutor - filename
[ ] Window size is persisted
[ ] "-" in site.key plays that MIDI number
[ ] Custom tones persist and appear in the instrument list
[ ] No ABC anywhere


17. IMPLEMENTATION NOTES FOR ANOTHER MODEL
------------------------------------------
Write one file. Prefer explicit pygame drawing over GUI frameworks.
Keep staff math in helpers: spell_midi, staff_y_spelled, draw_key_signature.
Drive song quiz from the same grouped-event timeline as playback
(play_beat / quiz_beat).
Treat duration as both spawn spacing (when generating) and notehead shape
(when drawing).
Persist every control the user can change.